error[SC0531]: `from` on `Load` could be 2 implementations of `From`
  --> tests/ui/types/ambiguous_instances.science:26:10
   |
18 |     def from(value: I64) -> Self:
   |         ---- one accepts `I64`
...
22 |     def from(value: F64) -> Self:
   |         ---- one accepts `F64`
...
26 |     Load.from(1)
   |          ^^^^ supplied an integer literal, which fits all of them
   |
   = note: these are one method at several instantiations of one interface, so the argument types are what choose between them — and here they did not narrow it to one
   = note: a literal or `null` has no type until a signature expects one, and which signature that is is what this call is trying to decide — give the argument a type first, with a suffix or a binding that is annotated
